From cdfad4aed8b8e3ddcaddee3f8f2a9398f9db9c34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:42:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/rtpdec_rfc4175: Return no packet when the first
 field ends

rfc4175_finalize_packet() returned success without a packet for the first
field of interlaced video, so an empty packet was returned for every frame.

This is not a security issue.

Fixes: 1l09F1Fvpg1j
Empty packets Replicated through API
Found during triage of the security report V8a3e2cGQI7w, also raised by Forgejo Fairy while reviewing PR #24949

(cherry picked from commit cdfad4aed8b8e3ddcaddee3f8f2a9398f9db9c34)
---
 libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c b/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c
index 41bf4a2c5dc..3d31bb268bb 100644
--- a/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c
+++ b/libavformat/rtpdec_rfc4175.c
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ fail:
 static int rfc4175_finalize_packet(PayloadContext *data, AVPacket *pkt,
                                    int stream_index)
 {
-    int ret = 0;
+    int ret = AVERROR(EAGAIN);
 
     pkt->stream_index = stream_index;
     if (!data->interlaced || data->field) {
-- 
2.53.0

